  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Holding On**: rare: 13 archived performances [2]\n- **Chat**: rare: 14 archived performances [2]\n- **Chat**: rare: 14 archived performances [2]\n- **Hot Piss**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [2]\n- **Chat & Tuning**: rare: 12 archived performances [2]\n- **Straight Into Darkness**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [2]\n- **Thanks To The Crew**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [2]\n- **Chat/Raffle Draw**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [2]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **twod2018-12-21.SchoepsMK41.24bit** (recommended): source not stated; 20 songs; 115 min [1]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- Stage talk about: Chat/Raffle Draw/Tim Heidecker [1]\n- Paul Vile joined on harp, Tim Heidecker on lead vocals and acoustic guitar [1]\n- Frances Quinlan played tambourine alongside Adam Granduciel and Anthony LaMarca during the chat segment [1]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **twod2018-12-21.SchoepsMK41.24bit**: taped by Joe Burns; transferred by Dennis Orr; source: Schoeps MK41's supercardioids > Actives > Nbox > Roland R-07 @ 24 bit/48 kHz [1]. Also: Recorded with Schoeps MK41 supercardioid mics into a Roland R-07 recorder at 24-bit/48kHz [1]",
